{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep and do, for it is your wisdom and your understanding in the eyes of the peoples.</b> Scripture teaches you here that all the commandments depend on the commandments of keeping and doing, and all of them are included within them. For example, you would say that the wisdom of medicine is included in the Torah in the verse (Exodus 15:26): ״If you will diligently hearken to the voice of YHWH your Elohim, and do what is upright in His eyes, and give ear to His commandments and keep all His statutes — all the disease that I put upon Egypt I will not put upon you, for I am YHWH your healer״ — and so too all the other wisdoms. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״in the eyes of the peoples״ — which is the wisdom that is ״in the eyes of the peoples״? This is one who knows how to calculate seasons and constellations; and anyone who knows how to calculate them but does not do so — concerning him Scripture says (Isaiah 5:12): ״ואת פעל ה' לא יביטו ומעשה ידיו לא ראו״." "<b>All these statutes.</b> It should have said ״את כל המצות האלה״, for the nations do not praise and glorify Israel on account of the statutes; rather they mock them. But He mentioned the statutes in order to intensify and say: since the nations will see that Israel engages in rational commandments and in just laws that reason itself testifies are righteous laws, arranged in proper order and upright governance — it will become clear to them from this that the statutes, whose reason is not known, are not empty things, but rather there is within their inner being a great hidden wisdom that not all attain. And the nations themselves will glorify Israel for everything, and their praise will demand to say even concerning the statutes: ״רק עם חכם ונבון״ — surely a wise and understanding people. And the sense of רק is to exclude the other peoples."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:16.182240397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}